<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ reports NZ$150.2 mln trade surplus in June.</title>
<headline>NZ reports NZ$150.2 mln trade surplus in June.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics New Zealand on Thursday released the following provisional statistics for New Zealand external merchandise trade for June.</p>
<p>(Figures are rounded, with revised-from data in brackets)</p>
<p>Monthly series:</p>
<p>		June 1997	   May 1997		  June 1996</p>
<p>Balance    +$150.2 million	 +$413.6 million(406.5)  +$8.8 million</p>
<p>Exports     $1.82 billion     $2.09 bln	     $1.65 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.67 billion     $1.68 bln	     $1.64 bln</p>
<p>		Yr-to-June 1997 Yr-to-May 1997     Yr-to-June 1996</p>
<p>Balance    -$275.7 million     -$417.1 million(-$460.6) -$806.7 million</p>
<p>Exports     $21.05 bln	$20.88 bln ($20.84)  $20.55 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $21.33 bln	$21.30 bln	     $21.35 bln</p>
<p>Trend series:</p>
<p>		June 1997	    May 1997	     June 1996</p>
<p>Balance    +$27.7 million	-$14.8 (-$158.1)	-$46.6 million</p>
<p>Exports     $1.77 billion  $1.75 bln		 $1.75 bln</p>
<p>Imports     $1.75 billion  $1.76 bln ($1.83)     $1.80 bln</p>
<p>For the June quarter, the balance was in surplus $646.5 million, up from $52.3 million in the March quarter and against a June quarter 1996 surplus of $458.4 million, SNZ added.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
